Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 22:21:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02690/11362] [outer-loop] Live submission needs a CUDA
 llama-server BINARY (MTP is in libllama-common), not a wheel +
 CARNOT_LLAMA_SERVER env

Answer to 'do we need a wheel for llama.cpp+MTP?': NO -- a BINARY. Verified MTP
(common_speculative_impl_draft_mtp) lives in libllama-common (30 symbols) NOT core libllama (0); the
llama-server binary links it and LocalGGUFProposer launches that binary. The stock llama-cpp-python wheel
wraps only core libllama + its own python speculative decoding -> CANNOT do native --spec-type draft-mtp.
So bundle the CUDA-compiled llama-server + shared libs (incl. libllama-common) as a Kaggle Dataset; the
binary is model-agnostic (loads the GGUF at runtime). Added CARNOT_LLAMA_SERVER env override to
_resolve_llama_server so the submission points at the bundled binary. Manifest updated: build recipe
(CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=75;89 for T4/L4, build in a Kaggle notebook for toolkit match) + the wheel
fallback (no MTP, CARNOT_ARC_MTP=0). ruff clean; env override tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
